WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.790
Some ideas are too interesting to leave in a notes file. Give them a little garden.

2
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:11.200
These are real projects. Scriptorium studies how a text is written. Quillgrain carries its voice.

3
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:18.070
From them, local Gemma grew Echo Cartography: a map of how that voice changes from draft to draft.

4
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:24.290
An editor could use it to spot unwanted changes. Keep the possibility, with both its roots.

5
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:30.620
Other sprouts can become ingredients, too. Here are two earlier discoveries, ready for another turn.

6
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.900
Send them back to the pile. Their words become new scraps, still connected to the ideas that grew them.

7
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:42.590
Nothing is lost. The originals stay, and a new combination can take the idea further.

8
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:48.850
Your ideas, on your device. A little messy. A little magical. Let your wild ideas ferment.
